        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e079f48a-f8a6-5d43-b90b-8e21cb6d690c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Daniel Craig, Terence Gross, Toni Collette, Stephen Tompkinson, Joseph Stalin\n- Films: Hotel Splendide, Casino Royale, Brassed Off, Archangel\n- Roles: James Bond, Dr. Christopher \"Fluke\" Kelso\n- Topics: British independent dark comedy film, Soviet history\n\nFacts:\n- In 1996, Stephen Tompkinson starred in the film Brassed Off.\n- In 2000, Hotel Splendide was released as a British independent dark comedy film written and directed by Terence Gross and starring Toni Collette and Daniel Craig.\n- In 2000, Stephen Tompkinson also starred in the film Hotel Splendide.\n- In 2005, Daniel Craig played Dr. Christopher \"Fluke\" Kelso in Archangel, a character who is an English expert on Soviet history in Moscow for a conference on Joseph Stalin.\n- In October 2005, Daniel Craig was cast as the British secret agent James Bond.\n- In November 2006, Daniel Craig's first James Bond film, Casino Royale, was released internationally.",
